rror":false,"num_turns":21,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've finished PKT-0075 and committed it. The change is delivered as a patch plus a decision note under `.theseus/diagnosis/`, because there is no writable fork of Euro-Office/DocumentServer yet. It has not gone through a real `dpkg -i` of a rebuilt package or a Docker image build.\n\n**What the patch does** (`PKT-0075-js-snapshots-install.patch`, explained in `PKT-0075-js-snapshots-install.md`):\n- **Generates the snapshots at install and upgrade:** `documentserver-generate-allfonts.sh` now runs `x2t -create-js-snapshots` right after the existing `-create-js-cache` step.\n- **Clears stale snapshots:** it deletes `sdkjs/*/sdk-all.bin` before generating, and again if x2t fails. So after an upgrade there is either a fresh snapshot or none, never one from an older build. A failure prints a warning; the install still succeeds and x2t runs without snapshots, as it does today.\n- **Owner `ds`:** the script already runs `chown -R ds:ds sdkjs` afterwards, so the files belong to `ds` even though the install runs as root.\n- **Uninstall cleanup:** `postrm` now also deletes `sdk-all.bin`, since these files aren't in the package's file list.\n\n**Decisions**\n- I put the change in that one script because the deb install, the deb upgrade, the font-change trigger and Docker start-up all run it, so one hunk covers every case. That Euro-Office's Docker start-up calls this script is an assumption based on the upstream ONLYOFFICE start-up script; I couldn't check it here.\n- I rejected shipping prebuilt `.bin` files in the package: each snapshot only works with the exact x2t/V8 build and `sdk-all.js` it was made from.\n\n**Proof on the VM:** I ran the patched script as root, the way the install does. All five `sdk-all.bin` files were recreated and owned by `ds`, and the whole script took 55 s. `/healthcheck` still returns `true`. A docx → pdf conversion as `ds` succeeded in 0.51 s, in line with PKT-0065's \"with snapshots\" figure. The VM now has these regenerated files; the old copies are in the session scratchpad.\n\n**Acceptance:** `npm run lint:check` passes. `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` passed on the final run, but it fails intermittently: three runs in a row gave pass, fail, pass, with one test failing in `tests/unit/docsCoServerCrashPaths.tests.js`. That isn't caused by this packet, which changes no JavaScript. I recorded a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/` to fix the flaky test.\n\nThe Executor log, the friction line and the Atlas lesson are written, and `theseus validate` reports 0 errors.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas (x2t):** everything generated at install time (AllFonts, themes, js cache and now the snapshots) comes from `documentserver-generate-allfonts.sh`. That script is the place to hook anything tied to the exact x2t/sdkjs build.","ttft_ms":2176,"type":"result","duration_ms":231496,"uuid":"55a61e90-4098-4624-9a6c-198bccb36374","ttft_stream_ms":1072,"time_to_request_ms":427,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":309,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":5,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":13,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":21,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":4,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":38,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":161,"time_to_request_major_faults":6,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":236,"process_anon_mib_result":145,"process_peak_rss_mib":251,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3767,"process_wall_ms_turn":231496,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1281,"process_wall_ms_streaming":72494,"main_stream_count":21,"main_stream_event_count":1507,"main_str